#!/usr/bin/env -S sh -c 'exec "$(dirname "$0")/../../.github/scripts/ety_case_study" "$0" "$@"'
%% -*- erlang -*-
%% Case study manifest, see .github/scripts/ety_case_study.
%%
%% src and include of the hex package prometheus 4.8.1, the one antidote_stats depends on (checksum
%% as in the lock file of antidote_stats at antidote commit ed9cfbcaad53c9b5de15bfcef7befef44b5b4221):
%% the modules, in the subdirectories that src has in the package, and the two headers. The code is
%% unchanged; 22 declarations (-spec, -type, -export_type) that were wrong or too imprecise are
%% corrected, see the list below.
%% Of the 30 modules 29 are in the study, with 471 functions. prometheus_model.erl (233 functions)
%% is generated by gpb and only there because the records of prometheus_model.hrl refer to its
%% types. The only dependency is quantile_estimator, see quantile_estimator.study:
%% prometheus_quantile_summary includes its header and calls it.
%%
%% 67 of the 471 functions have a spec in the source; the six metric modules (243 functions) have
%% none. overlay_prometheus.erl gives a spec to each of the other 404, and every module is checked
%% with it, so that a call into another module of prometheus is checked against the spec of the
%% callee. The specs follow the types of the modules and of the headers, the callbacks of the
%% behaviours and the edoc comments of the package: the functions of the metric modules take the
%% documented arguments (a name, a list of label values, a number), not term().
%%
%% With the specs alone 333 functions type check and 138 do not. With the declarations as the package
%% has them it is 316 and 155 (and 422 and 49 without the overlay, where a function without a spec
%% is dynamic()). The corrections make 17 functions type check: collect_mf/2 of the six collectors;
%% duration_unit_from_string/1, from_native/2 and to_native/2 of prometheus_time; create_mf/4,
%% label_pair/1, metrics_from_tuples/2, summary_metric/1 and summary_metric/4 of
%% prometheus_model_helpers; prometheus_mnesia:table_path/3, prometheus_registry:exists/1 and
%% prometheus_text_format:join/2. Four functions of prometheus_model_helpers get a correct spec and
%% fail with another first error: metric_name/1, metric_from_tuple/2, ensure_list/1 and
%% ensure_binary_or_string/1. No function fails that type checked before.
%%
%% Library specs, flags and assertions (step IV). 431 functions type check as they are, 16 with a flag
%% (13 without the redundancy check of their clauses, 3 without the exhaustiveness check), 24 are
%% ignored; 169 assertions (160 assert_type, 7 assert_pattern, 2 annotate_type) in 25 modules. Each
%% flag and each assertion is needed: without it exactly its function fails. The source of each of
%% the 24 was read, no exception has the reason unknown.
%%   overlay_prometheus_lib.erl has 16 specs for functions of OTP and is on the 20 modules that call
%%     one of them. They say more than OTP does for element/2 (typed by the tuple for a pair and for
%%     the row of a metric family), integer_to_list/1, lists:map/2 (a list that is not empty stays
%%     so), keyfind/3, seq/2, sum/1 and flatten/1 and for proplists:delete/2. Where OTP gives a result
%%     as a type variable that is bound only in when, and that so fits every type, they say term():
%%     application:get_env/2,3 and get_key/2 and ets:select/2; lists:foldl/3 and foldr/3 bind the
%%     accumulator. erlang:system_info/1 and erlang:statistics/1 have the items that prometheus asks
%%     for, 7 clauses each where OTP has 81 and 19: with the 81
%%     prometheus_vm_system_info_collector:allocators/0 ran into the timeout (and was accepted with
%%     more time, wrongly), and a match on a result of erlang:statistics/1, which OTP gives with type
%%     variables, counted as dead.
%%     mnesia_tm:get_info/1, ram_file:open/2 and ram_file:get_size/1 have no spec in OTP, and for
%%     such a function the checker takes none from an overlay: three name errors stay.
%%   The overlay alone makes 9 functions type check: schedulers_seq/0 of the counter, the histogram
%%     and the two summaries, prometheus_histogram:buckets_seq/1, mf_labels/1, mf_constant_labels/1
%%     and mf_duration_unit/1 of prometheus_metric and prometheus_mnesia:table_disk_size/2. With
%%     term() for the application environment 8 functions that type checked before need an
%%     assertion (reason app_env): prometheus_collector:collect_mf/3, prometheus_sup:default_metrics/0
%%     and enabled_metrics/0 of the six collectors.
%%   Flags: 13 functions have clauses that are dead for their spec, a clause that raises an error for
%%     a value outside the documented types (defensive). 3 lack a clause:
%%     prometheus_text_format:emit_metric/3 for a metric without a value,
%%     prometheus_histogram:create_histogram_metric/6 for a list of less than two, and
%%     prometheus_quantile_summary:quantile/1, whose pattern is on a map of a type that is not
%%     supported.
%%   An assertion is an unchecked cast (assert_type, assert_pattern) of a value whose type the checker
%%     cannot know: what an ets table holds, the data of a metric family, a property of a spec, a
%%     value of the application environment, an item of mnesia or of the allocators, a field of a
%%     generated record, a value that the program has validated. 22 of them are for gaps of the
%%     checker (narrowing, map types, the range of a sum, a segment of a binary, a record guard): they
%%     say what is true and the checker does not see. The 2 annotate_type are checked: they give the
%%     subject of a case a wider type, so that a defensive branch is not dead. A function that also
%%     has an error in the program gets no assertion and stays ignored.
%%   Ignored: 7 for an error in the program (reasons source_bug and missing_fields): the two of
%%     prometheus_model_helpers and prometheus_quantile_summary:quantile_merge/2 as before, and four
%%     that an inherent first error had hidden: prometheus_boolean:save_toggle/3,
%%     prometheus_histogram:observe/4 and pobserve/6 and
%%     prometheus_quantile_summary:invariant_and_quantiles_from_spec/1. 3 of prometheus_gauge for
%%     the two values of a row (union_elimination). 14 for the checker: 3 specs
%%     with a map type that it rejects, 3 calls of OTP functions without a spec, fun hd/1, 2 for a
%%     bounded type variable, 1 for a pattern with a bound variable, 2 that need an assertion inside
%%     a fun and 2 that need one where the assertion crashes the engine.
%%
%% Declarations corrected in the source: 22 in 11 modules, old -> new. Only -spec, -type and
%% -export_type (the package declares no record outside the generated header); no function body,
%% clause head, guard, macro or comment, and neither of the headers. Where the overlay repeats a
%% type of the source (duration_unit(), help()) or names what a corrected spec takes (the type of a
%% metric family, the table of prometheus_mnesia:table_path/3) it follows.
%%
%% A type that does not exist, or is not exported:
%%   collect_mf/2 of the six collectors (prometheus_mnesia_collector, prometheus_vm_dist_collector,
%%     prometheus_vm_memory_collector, prometheus_vm_msacc_collector,
%%     prometheus_vm_statistics_collector, prometheus_vm_system_info_collector): Callback ::
%%     prometheus_collector:callback() -> prometheus_collector:collect_mf_callback(), the type that
%%     the callback collect_mf/2 of the behaviour has. The checker ended with an internal error for
%%     each of the six.
%%   prometheus_model_helpers: -export_type gets label_value/0, which status_class() of
%%     prometheus_http names. The checker accepts a remote type that is not exported: no verdict
%%     changes.
%%
%% Types that say something else than the code does:
%%   prometheus_metric: duration_unit() gets hours, a unit that prometheus_time has
%%     (?DURATION_UNITS, from_native/2, to_native/2) and documents.
%%   prometheus_metric: help() binary() | nonempty_string() -> binary() | string().
%%     prometheus_metric_spec:validate_metric_help/1 accepts "", and the examples in the
%%     documentation of prometheus_time have {help, ""}. No verdict changes.
%%   prometheus_metric: result of maybe_set_default/4 ok -> any(). The first clause gives what
%%     set_default/2 of the metric module gives, for which the callback says any(): it is a
%%     boolean() (ets:insert_new/2) in five of the six. The call is Module:set_default(..), which
%%     the checker does not see: no verdict changes.
%%   prometheus_model_helpers: metric_name/1, result iolist() -> iodata(), and the elements of a
%%     list char() | .. -> byte() | ... An atom and a binary give a binary; a list comes back with
%%     its atoms replaced, and ?METRIC_NAME puts the result into the iolist that is the name for
%%     create_mf/4 ("Why iolists do not support atoms?", says the documentation).
%%   prometheus_model_helpers: result of ensure_binary_or_string/1 binary() | string() ->
%%     binary() | iolist(). It is written to the fields name and value of #'LabelPair'{} and name
%%     and help of #'MetricFamily'{}, which are iodata(); the last clause gives a deep list
%%     (io_lib:format/2), and prometheus_text_format:escape_label_value/1 takes binary() | iolist()
%%     for a label value.
%%   prometheus_model_helpers: summary() gets {Count, Sum, Quantiles} and {Labels, Count, Sum,
%%     Quantiles} with the quantiles as [{number(), value()}], the tuples of the first two clauses
%%     of summary_metric/1.
%%   prometheus_mnesia: table_disk_size/1 and table_disk_size/2, Table :: file:name_all() ->
%%     file:name(). table_path/3 puts the table into a list with the extension, and in a list a
%%     file name takes no binary.
%%   prometheus_text_format: join/2, List1 :: [T] -> [T, ...]. It is lists:join/2 of OTP without
%%     the clause for [].
%%
%% Types that say too little:
%%   prometheus_registry: exists/1 (atom() | iolist()) -> boolean() | atom() becomes (atom()) ->
%%     boolean(); (iolist()) -> atom(). The clause for an iolist calls exists/1 with an atom and
%%     matches the result with true and false.
%%   prometheus_model_helpers: create_mf/4 and create_mf/5, Type :: atom() -> gauge | counter |
%%     summary | histogram | untyped | boolean, the atoms that ensure_mf_type/1 and
%%     metric_from_tuple/2 have clauses for.
%%   prometheus_model_helpers: result of ensure_mf_type/1 atom() -> prometheus_model:'MetricType'(),
%%     for the field type of #'MetricFamily'{}.
%%   prometheus_model_helpers: summary_metric/4, Quantiles :: list() -> [{number(), value()}], the
%%     pairs that the #'Quantile'{} records are made of.
%%   prometheus_model_helpers: ensure_list/1 (term()) -> list() becomes ([T] | T) -> [T], so that
%%     metrics_from_tuples/2 keeps the type of the metrics. The function does not type check with it
%%     either, see its exception.
%%
%% Left as they are:
%%   prometheus_metric:name() (atom() | binary() | nonempty_string() | iolist()) serves two uses: the
%%     name in the spec of a metric, where validate_metric_name/2 accepts a list only if it is a
%%     string, and the name that the collectors give to create_mf/4, an iolist (?METRIC_NAME). It
%%     is true for both and exact for neither. With name() without iolist() and Name ::
%%     prometheus_metric:name() | iolist() in create_mf/4,5, prometheus_metric_spec:to_string/1 type
%%     checks and nothing else changes (measured, not applied).
%%   prometheus_buckets: exponential/3 and linear/3, (number(), number(), pos_integer()) -> buckets(),
%%     are true: for a positive count the list is not empty. The checker cannot see that (reason
%%     nonempty_list). With the result [number()] the next error is the clause for Count < 1; with
%%     Count :: integer() as well both type check (measured, not applied).
%%   prometheus_metric:value(), the result of the callbacks value/1,2,3, has neither the boolean()
%%     that prometheus_boolean gives nor the {Count, Sum, Quantiles} of prometheus_quantile_summary.
%%     No function is checked against a callback.
%%   prometheus_model.hrl and prometheus_model.erl are generated (reason model_field, and partial for
%%     prometheus_text_format:emit_metric/3).
%%   Where the program is wrong, see the exceptions with the reasons source_bug and missing_fields.

{study, prometheus}.
{deps, ["quantile_estimator"]}.

%% {reason, Id, Class, Text}. Class: real (the program or its spec is wrong), inherent (correct at
%% run time, not provable by types), fixable (gap in the type system or checker), benign (dead for the spec, kept on purpose), unknown.
%% The reason of an exception with ignore is the one of what blocks the function in the end: the first error that no
%% library spec, flag or assertion takes away without hiding a real error. Its comment names what is in front of it and
%% behind it. The reason of an assertion is the one of the value that it casts, the reason of a flag the one of the
%% clauses.
{reason, ets_value,            inherent, "what an ets table holds is not in its type: ets:lookup/2 gives [tuple()], for a set it is [] or one row of the shape the module inserts; ets:select_replace/2 for one key gives 0 or 1; ets:select/2 and ets:lookup_element/3 give terms; ets:match/2 gives the bindings of a row as a list of terms (prometheus_metric:metrics/2, load_all_values/2,3 of the metric modules); element/2 of a row whose size depends on the metric gives a term()"}.
{reason, mf_data,              inherent, "prometheus_metric:mf_data/1 gives the data of a metric, a term() (prometheus_collector:data()): each metric module knows what it has stored there, the buckets or the configuration"}.
{reason, proplist,             inherent, "term() from a property list (proplists:get_value/2,3 on the spec of a metric, on erlang:memory/0), used at the type of the property"}.
{reason, app_env,              inherent, "term() from the application environment (application:get_env/2,3, application:get_key/2), used at the type that the configuration of prometheus has"}.
{reason, info_item,            inherent, "mnesia:system_info/1 and mnesia:table_info/2 give term(): the type depends on the item asked for. Where the call is in a fun, the fun is cast as a whole (nothing in a fun can carry an assertion), which leaves its body unchecked against the type"}.
{reason, info_arg,             fixable,  "erlang:system_info/1, erlang:port_info/2 or erlang:process_info/2 called with an atom() that the program knows is an item: one of those that the metrics of the collector name"}.
{reason, alloc_info,           inherent, "the allocator information of erlang:system_info({allocator, A}) is a nested property list of terms"}.
{reason, model_field,          inherent, "a field of a record of prometheus_model.hrl, which gpb generates, read at the type that prometheus_model_helpers writes: the field is optional (T | undefined), a number can also be infinity, '-infinity' or nan, the type of a metric family an integer()"}.
{reason, validated,            inherent, "a term that the program validates at run time (a regular expression, io_lib:printable_unicode_list/1, lists:any/2), used at the validated type"}.
{reason, unchecked_result,     inherent, "a result that can be false or undefined, used as the success value: lists:keyfind/3 for a key that the program knows is there, erlang:process_info/2, erlang:port_info/2, erlang:statistics(microstate_accounting), prometheus_metric:check_mf_exists/3"}.
{reason, body_exhaustiveness,  inherent, "exhaustiveness of a match or a case inside the body: the program lets it crash for the other values"}.
{reason, partial,              inherent, "partial function, the callers rule out the missing case"}.
{reason, defensive,            benign,   "defensive clause, dead for the spec. As an annotation, which is checked: the subject of a case that has such a branch, at a wider type, so that the checker takes the branch as reachable"}.
{reason, nonempty_list,        inherent, "a list that the program knows is not empty: a result typed [T, ...] for a positive count, the counters of the buckets of a histogram, the rows of a series that a query has found (so that a fold over them does not give its initial value)"}.
{reason, list_shape,           inherent, "the shape of a list that a list type cannot say: a list of two, a list that starts with two sums, a row as a list of elements of different types"}.
{reason, improper_list,        inherent, "a guard is_list/1 holds for an improper list too, the program takes the list to be a proper one"}.
{reason, correlated,           inherent, "the type of a value depends on another value, which the types of two variables cannot say: the metric of prometheus_model_helpers:metric_from_tuple/2 is of the kind that its first argument names"}.
{reason, union_elimination,    fixable,  "variables bound from a union of tuples lose their correlation (etylizer#28)"}.
{reason, number_range,         fixable,  "range of a number that the types do not show: erlang:convert_time_unit/3 of one second is positive"}.
{reason, text_bytes,           fixable,  "text that is typed string() or io_lib:chars(), whose characters need not be bytes, used as iodata(): here it is ASCII, the name of a metric type or a number as io_lib:format/2 and float_to_list/1 print it"}.
{reason, start_ret,            fixable,  "result of starting the supervisor: supervisor:start_link/3 can give ignore, init/1 of the module does not"}.
{reason, catch_value,          fixable,  "the value of catch Expr is a term()"}.
{reason, missing_fields,       real,     "a record is built without fields whose types have no undefined"}.
{reason, source_bug,           real,     "error in the program"}.
{reason, otp_no_spec,          fixable,  "calls an OTP function that has no spec, which is a name error; a spec in a library overlay is not taken for such a function"}.
{reason, bif_fun,              fixable,  "fun hd/1: a fun that names an auto-imported BIF without its module is a name error"}.
{reason, map_types,            fixable,  "map types with more than one association or with mandatory associations are not supported: a spec that has one is rejected; behind a type alias a pattern on a map of that type does not count as matching it, and a map expression is not of the type. As an assertion or a flag: the pattern of a match or of a clause on such a map, for a key that the type has; a map expression cast to the type; the value under a key that is a variable"}.
{reason, narrowing,            fixable,  "a type test does not narrow: X =:= all on the left of orelse for the right, a filter X =/= undefined in a comprehension, a case on is_atom(X) for its branches"}.
{reason, nonempty_seq,         fixable,  "a list mapped from lists:seq(0, N - 1) with N > 0, or built by a recursion that counts down from N > 0, is not empty"}.
{reason, type_predicate,       fixable,  "narrowing by a predicate: case io_lib:printable_unicode_list(X) of true gives a string() X"}.
{reason, record_guard,         fixable,  "a guard is_record(X, r) narrows X to tuple() and counts as true for every tuple, not only for #r{}"}.
{reason, arith_range,          fixable,  "the sum of integers with a range has none: pos_integer() + 1 and 5 + non_neg_integer() are not a pos_integer()"}.
{reason, bit_segment,          fixable,  "an integer segment of a binary pattern is integer(), its size gives no range: <<X:8>> is not a byte()"}.
{reason, bounded_tyvar,        fixable,  "a type variable with a bound in when (Value :: T) counts as T itself: a fun argument over the variable must take all of T"}.
{reason, bound_pattern,        fixable,  "a pattern with an already bound variable is not handled: the case counts as not exhaustive, no assertion closes it"}.
{reason, in_fun,               fixable,  "needs an assertion inside a fun, which the assertions do not reach (assertions:visit/4 skips the clauses of a fun)"}.
{reason, assertion_crash,      fixable,  "needs an assertion that crashes the engine: assertions:hash/1 fails when the hash of an expression at the position is a code point"}.
{reason, spec_imprecise, real, "imprecise type spec in the source"}.
{reason, spec_wrong, real, "wrong type in the source"}.

%% Library specs that overlays correct
{correction, erlang, system_info, 1, spec_wrong}. % {allocator, A} -> [_], documented false | undefined
{correction, erlang, integer_to_list, 1, spec_imprecise}.
{correction, lists, foldl, 3, spec_imprecise}.
{correction, lists, foldr, 3, spec_imprecise}.
{correction, lists, map, 2, spec_imprecise}.
{correction, lists, seq, 2, spec_imprecise}.
{correction, lists, sum, 1, spec_imprecise}.

{module, prometheus, #{file => "prometheus/src/prometheus.erl",
                       overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.
%% start/2: prometheus_sup:start_link(), supervisor:start_link/3, gives ignore only if init/1 does, and
%% prometheus_sup:init/1 gives {ok, ..}
{assertion, prometheus, {19, 34, "4f8d28"}, assert_type, "{ok, pid()} | {error, term()}", start_ret}.

{module, prometheus_buckets, #{file => "prometheus/src/prometheus_buckets.erl",
                               overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"},
                                            {library, "overlay_prometheus_lib.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.
%% the clause for undefined and the last clause, for what is not a list: dead for the four forms of buckets that the
%% spec has. (In front of them, in step III: lists:last(Buckets) of the lists:map/2 of a list that is not empty, which
%% the library spec now says)
{exception, prometheus_buckets, new, 1, [no_redundancy], defensive}.
%% the first clause, for a Count below 1: dead for pos_integer()
{exception, prometheus_buckets, exponential, 3, [no_redundancy], defensive}.
%% exponential/3: a comprehension over lists:seq(0, Count - 1), which is not empty for the pos_integer() Count
{assertion, prometheus_buckets, {100, 3, "3761ed"}, assert_type, "[number(), ...]", nonempty_seq}.
%% the first clause, for a Count below 1: dead for pos_integer()
{exception, prometheus_buckets, linear, 3, [no_redundancy], defensive}.
%% linear/3: linear/4 gives [] only for the count 0, and Count is a pos_integer()
{assertion, prometheus_buckets, {118, 3, "ea94cf"}, assert_type, "[number(), ...]", nonempty_seq}.

{module, prometheus_collector, #{file => "prometheus/src/prometheus_collector.erl",
                                 overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"},
                                              {library, "overlay_prometheus_lib.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.
%% enabled_collectors/0: {ok, Collectors} = application:get_env(prometheus, collectors), the configured collectors,
%% where default stands for the collectors of the package
{assertion, prometheus_collector, {136, 52, "3922b2"}, assert_type, "[collector() | default]", app_env}.
%% collect_mf/3: {ok, Labels0} = application:get_env(prometheus, global_labels), the labels for every metric. Type
%% checked without it as long as the result of application:get_env/2 fitted every type
{assertion, prometheus_collector, {149, 53, "546280"}, assert_type, "prometheus_model_helpers:labels()", app_env}.

{module, prometheus_format, #{file => "prometheus/src/prometheus_format.erl",
                              overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.

{module, prometheus_instrumenter, #{file => "prometheus/src/prometheus_instrumenter.erl",
                                    overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"},
                                                 {library, "overlay_prometheus_lib.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.
%% enabled_instrumenters/0: {ok, Instrumenters} = application:get_env(prometheus, instrumenters)
{assertion, prometheus_instrumenter, {29, 28, "e25831"}, assert_type, "[instrumenter()]", app_env}.

{module, prometheus_metric, #{file => "prometheus/src/prometheus_metric.erl",
                              overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"},
                                           {library, "overlay_prometheus_lib.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.
%% check_mf_exists/4: case ets:lookup(Table, {Registry, mf, Name}) of [] -> ..; [{_, {Labels, _}, _, _, _} = MF] -> ..
%% end. The table is a set: no row, or the one that insert_mf/3 has written
{assertion, prometheus_metric, {141, 8, "7d17e5"}, assert_type, "[] | etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:mf(), [])", ets_value}.
%% check_mf_exists/3: case ets:lookup(Table, {Registry, mf, Name}) of [] -> ..; [MF] -> .. end
{assertion, prometheus_metric, {156, 8, "7d17e5"}, assert_type, "[] | etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:mf(), [])", ets_value}.

{module, prometheus_metric_spec, #{file => "prometheus/src/prometheus_metric_spec.erl",
                                   overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"},
                                                {library, "overlay_prometheus_lib.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.
%% registry/1: the key registry of the spec, the name of a registry
{assertion, prometheus_metric_spec, {35, 3, "7a6d5b"}, assert_type, "prometheus_registry:registry()", proplist}.
%% validate_metric_name/1: validate_metric_name(RawName, RawName) for a list, as the name and as its text:
%% validate_metric_name/2 raises an error unless it is a string (io_lib:printable_unicode_list/1, re:run/2)
{assertion, prometheus_metric_spec, {136, 24, "469ad2"}, assert_type, "string()", validated}.
{assertion, prometheus_metric_spec, {136, 33, "469ad2"}, assert_type, "string()", validated}.
%% lists:map(fun validate_metric_label_name/1, RawLabels) behind the guard is_list(RawLabels), which holds for an
%% improper list too: wants an assertion [term()] (improper_list) on RawLabels at 159:47, the only expression that can
%% carry it, and its hash is 0d225c. With the variable renamed in a scratch copy the assertion gets the function through
{exception, prometheus_metric_spec, validate_metric_label_names, 1, [ignore], assertion_crash}.
%% validate_metric_label_name/1: RawName, a list for which io_lib:printable_unicode_list/1 has said true
{assertion, prometheus_metric_spec, {171, 42, "469ad2"}, assert_type, "string()", type_predicate}.
%% validate_metric_help/1: RawHelp, a list for which io_lib:printable_unicode_list/1 has said true
{assertion, prometheus_metric_spec, {197, 14, "aa7094"}, assert_type, "string()", type_predicate}.
%% to_string/1: Value, a name() that is a list. name() has iolist() too, but the name of a spec has passed
%% validate_metric_name/2, which accepts a list only if it is a string
{assertion, prometheus_metric_spec, {209, 3, "2caa2e"}, assert_type, "string()", validated}.

{module, prometheus_misc, #{file => "prometheus/src/prometheus_misc.erl",
                            overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"},
                                         {library, "overlay_prometheus_lib.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.
%% all_module_attributes/1: the key modules of an application is the list of its modules
{assertion, prometheus_misc, {36, 29, "e1023a"}, assert_type, "undefined | {ok, [module()]}", app_env}.
%% module_attributes/1: case catch Module:module_info(attributes) of ..; V -> V end. What is not an 'EXIT' tuple is the
%% list of the attributes
{assertion, prometheus_misc, {54, 7, "e91551"}, assert_type, "[{atom(), [term()]}]", catch_value}.

{module, prometheus_registry, #{file => "prometheus/src/prometheus_registry.erl",
                                overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.
%% collect/2: {_, Collector} <- ets:lookup(?TABLE, Registry). The table is a bag of {Registry, Collector}, as
%% register_collector/2 inserts them
{assertion, prometheus_registry, {86, 23, "3876a5"}, assert_type, "[{registry(), prometheus_collector:collector()}]", ets_value}.
%% collectors/1: {_, Collector} <- ets:lookup(?TABLE, Registry), as in collect/2
{assertion, prometheus_registry, {95, 35, "3876a5"}, assert_type, "[{registry(), prometheus_collector:collector()}]", ets_value}.

{module, prometheus_sup, #{file => "prometheus/src/prometheus_sup.erl",
                           overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"},
                                        {library, "overlay_prometheus_lib.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.
%% default_metrics/0: application:get_env(prometheus, default_metrics, []), a list of {Type, Spec} and {Registry, Type,
%% Spec}. Type checked without it as long as the result of application:get_env/3 fitted every type
{assertion, prometheus_sup, {78, 3, "dd9629"}, assert_type, "[overlay_prometheus:metric_decl()]", app_env}.

{module, prometheus_time, #{file => "prometheus/src/prometheus_time.erl",
                            overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.
%% validate_duration_unit/1: SDU, the term of the key duration_unit of a spec, which lists:any/2 has found among the
%% units of ?DURATION_UNITS
{assertion, prometheus_time, {128, 7, "e5bd7e"}, assert_type, "prometheus_metric:duration_unit()", validated}.

{module, prometheus_mnesia_collector, #{file => "prometheus/src/collectors/mnesia/prometheus_mnesia_collector.erl",
                                        overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"},
                                                     {library, "overlay_prometheus_lib.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.
%% metrics/1: fun() -> mnesia:system_info(transaction_failures) end and the three funs below it are DataFuns, which give
%% metrics: mnesia:system_info/1 gives term(), for these four items it is a counter. Nothing in a fun can carry an
%% assertion, the fun can; here it is the tuple around it, as the hash 0b2334 of the fun crashes the engine
{assertion, prometheus_mnesia_collector, {140, 4, "fd9711"}, assert_type, "{failed_transactions, counter, string(), fun(() -> non_neg_integer())}", info_item}.
{assertion, prometheus_mnesia_collector, {145, 5, "973e59"}, assert_type, "fun(() -> non_neg_integer())", info_item}.
{assertion, prometheus_mnesia_collector, {148, 5, "b19487"}, assert_type, "fun(() -> non_neg_integer())", info_item}.
{assertion, prometheus_mnesia_collector, {151, 5, "d1892c"}, assert_type, "fun(() -> non_neg_integer())", info_item}.
%% is_started/1: case [V || {A, _, V} <- application:which_applications(), A == App] of [] -> false; [_] -> true end. An
%% application is in the list once at most
{assertion, prometheus_mnesia_collector, {185, 8, "8008c6"}, assert_type, "[] | etylizer:cons(string(), [])", body_exhaustiveness}.
%% enabled_metrics/0: application:get_env(prometheus, mnesia_collector_metrics, all), the names of the enabled metrics
%% or all. Type checked without it as long as the result of application:get_env/3 fitted every type
{assertion, prometheus_mnesia_collector, {191, 3, "cbdf2a"}, assert_type, "all | [atom()]", app_env}.
%% metric_enabled/2: Metrics =:= all orelse lists:member(Name, Metrics): on the right of orelse Metrics is not all, so
%% it is the list
{assertion, prometheus_mnesia_collector, {194, 45, "ca81d3"}, assert_type, "[atom()]", narrowing}.
%% get_memory_usage/0: Calculator = fun(Tab, Sum) -> mnesia:table_info(Tab, memory) + Sum end: the memory of a table is
%% a number of words
{assertion, prometheus_mnesia_collector, {198, 16, "a45812"}, assert_type, "fun((atom(), non_neg_integer()) -> non_neg_integer())", info_item}.
%% get_memory_usage/0: mnesia:system_info(tables), the names of the tables
{assertion, prometheus_mnesia_collector, {201, 30, "d9a41d"}, assert_type, "[atom()]", info_item}.
%% mnesia:table_info(Tab, memory) * WordSize in the fun for lists:foldl/3: the term() of the info item wants an
%% assertion (info_item). A cast of the whole fun does not help here, the product with WordSize is checked all the same.
%% In front of it: mnesia:system_info(tables), which an assertion gets through
{exception, prometheus_mnesia_collector, get_tablewise_memory_usage, 0, [ignore], in_fun}.
%% get_tablewise_size/0: the fun gives mnesia:table_info(Tab, size), a term(), for each table: the number of its records
{assertion, prometheus_mnesia_collector, {216, 3, "a9dd8d"}, assert_type, "[{[{table, atom()}], non_neg_integer()}]", info_item}.
%% get_tablewise_size/0: mnesia:system_info(tables), the names of the tables
{assertion, prometheus_mnesia_collector, {216, 31, "d9a41d"}, assert_type, "[atom()]", info_item}.

{module, prometheus_vm_dist_collector, #{file => "prometheus/src/collectors/vm/prometheus_vm_dist_collector.erl",
                                         overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"},
                                                      {library, "overlay_prometheus_lib.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.
%% enabled_metrics/0: application:get_env(prometheus, vm_dist_collector_metrics, all), the names of the enabled metrics
%% or all. Type checked without it as long as the result of application:get_env/3 fitted every type
{assertion, prometheus_vm_dist_collector, {381, 3, "dcdb49"}, assert_type, "all | [atom()]", app_env}.
%% metric_enabled/2: Metrics =:= all orelse lists:member(Name, Metrics): on the right of orelse Metrics is not all, so
%% it is the list
{assertion, prometheus_vm_dist_collector, {384, 45, "ca81d3"}, assert_type, "[atom()]", narrowing}.
%% case proplists:get_value(address, Info, #net_address{}) of #net_address{..} -> .. end wants an assertion
%% #net_address{} (proplist) on the call at 396:10, whose hash is 0a4bd6. Behind it, seen with the variable renamed in a
%% scratch copy: the map #{dist_pid => DistPid, node_state => NodeState} as a dist_node(), which checks neither with its
%% two values asserted (map_types), and DistPid and NodeState, terms of the property list, as arguments of dist_info/5
{exception, prometheus_vm_dist_collector, dist_info, 2, [ignore], assertion_crash}.
%% dist_info/5: [DistPort] = [P || {P, I} <- AllPorts, ..]: the one port of the socket to the node. If there is none the
%% function fails, and metrics/0 gives [] for a failure
{assertion, prometheus_vm_dist_collector, {407, 5, "41a5d6"}, assert_pattern, "[_]", body_exhaustiveness}.
%% dist_info/5: proplists:get_value(name, I) behind the filter I =/= undefined: I is what erlang:port_info/1 gives, a
%% list or undefined
{assertion, prometheus_vm_dist_collector, {411, 35, "7adc31"}, assert_type, "[tuple()]", narrowing}.
%% dist_info/5: {ok, InetStats} = inet:getstat(DistPort), which can give {error, Posix}
{assertion, prometheus_vm_dist_collector, {414, 5, "330991"}, assert_pattern, "{ok, _}", body_exhaustiveness}.
%% dist_info/5: case erlang:port_info(DistPort, connected) of {_, DistPid} -> ..; {_, ConnectedPid} -> .. end: undefined
%% if the port is closed
{assertion, prometheus_vm_dist_collector, {415, 16, "acbeba"}, assert_type, "{connected, pid()}", unchecked_result}.
%% dist_info/5: Map#{inet_stats => InetStats, dist_port => DistPort, dist_pid => DistPid, node_state => NodeState} as a
%% dist_node(), a map type with several associations: a map expression of such a type does not check
{assertion, prometheus_vm_dist_collector, {419, 15, "7bef8f"}, assert_type, "overlay_prometheus:dist_node()", map_types}.
%% the spec has a map type with two associations
{exception, prometheus_vm_dist_collector, dist_tls_info, 1, [ignore], map_types}.
%% the spec has a map type with two associations
{exception, prometheus_vm_dist_collector, dist_tls_sender_info, 2, [ignore], map_types}.
%% metric/3: element(2, lists:keyfind(Key, 1, Stats)): the statistics of inet:getstat/1 have the key, one of the ten
%% options that metrics1/0 asks for
{assertion, prometheus_vm_dist_collector, {454, 37, "489f54"}, assert_type, "{atom(), integer()}", unchecked_result}.
%% metric/3: element(2, erlang:port_info(DistPort, Key)), which is undefined if the port is closed; the four items that
%% metrics1/0 asks for are integers
{assertion, prometheus_vm_dist_collector, {458, 37, "30baf3"}, assert_type, "{atom(), integer()}", unchecked_result}.
%% metric/3: Key, an atom(), as an item of erlang:port_info/2: one of those that metrics1/0 asks for
{assertion, prometheus_vm_dist_collector, {458, 64, "7e98e6"}, assert_type, "input | output | memory | queue_size", info_arg}.
%% metric_proc/3: element(2, process_info(Pid, Key)), which is undefined for a process that has ended; the eight items
%% that metrics1/0 asks for are integers
{assertion, prometheus_vm_dist_collector, {467, 59, "38c5f2"}, assert_type, "{atom(), integer()}", unchecked_result}.
%% metric_proc/3: Pid of the pattern #{PidKey := Pid} on a dist_node(), for the three keys of dist_pid_key(), whose
%% values are pids
{assertion, prometheus_vm_dist_collector, {467, 72, "9591bb"}, assert_type, "pid()", map_types}.
%% metric_proc/3: Key, an atom(), as an item of erlang:process_info/2: one of those that metrics1/0 asks for
{assertion, prometheus_vm_dist_collector, {467, 77, "7e98e6"}, assert_type, "memory | heap_size | min_heap_size | min_bin_vheap_size | stack_size | total_heap_size | message_queue_len | reductions", info_arg}.
%% metric_proc_status/2: proc_status(element(2, process_info(DistPid, status))): undefined for a process that has ended;
%% else the status, for which the spec of erlang:process_info/2 has the union of all its results
{assertion, prometheus_vm_dist_collector, {482, 36, "1b5ff1"}, assert_type, "{status, exiting | suspended | runnable | garbage_collecting | running | waiting}", unchecked_result}.
%% metric_proc_status/2: DistPid of the pattern #{PidKey := DistPid} on a dist_node(), as in metric_proc/3
{assertion, prometheus_vm_dist_collector, {482, 49, "880046"}, assert_type, "pid()", map_types}.
%% node_queue_size/1: ConnId = ets:lookup_element(sys_dist, Node, 3), the handle of the connection in the table of the
%% kernel, for erlang:dist_get_stat/1
{assertion, prometheus_vm_dist_collector, {507, 14, "59e78b"}, assert_type, "erlang:dist_handle()", ets_value}.
%% node_queue_size/1: case QueueSize of false -> 0; true -> -1; _ -> QueueSize end. The spec of erlang:dist_get_stat/1
%% has non_neg_integer() (a boolean() in older releases): the first two branches are dead. With the subject annotated,
%% which is checked, the checker takes them as reachable
{assertion, prometheus_vm_dist_collector, {509, 10, "27b792"}, annotate_type, "boolean() | non_neg_integer()", defensive}.

{module, prometheus_vm_memory_collector, #{file => "prometheus/src/collectors/vm/prometheus_vm_memory_collector.erl",
                                           overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"},
                                                        {library, "overlay_prometheus_lib.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.
%% metrics/0: get_value(atom, Data) - get_value(atom_used, Data) and the same for processes: proplists:get_value/2 on
%% Data = erlang:memory(), a list of {Type, Size} that has the keys asked for; each call gives a size, a number of
%% bytes. (The eight other calls of the function need no assertion: their values go into lists of metrics, and a list of
%% any terms is a prometheus_model_helpers:metrics(), as prometheus_boolean() has list())
{assertion, prometheus_vm_memory_collector, {129, 7, "22cfc0"}, assert_type, "non_neg_integer()", proplist}.
{assertion, prometheus_vm_memory_collector, {129, 31, "9ddc65"}, assert_type, "non_neg_integer()", proplist}.
{assertion, prometheus_vm_memory_collector, {151, 7, "6b5a4b"}, assert_type, "non_neg_integer()", proplist}.
{assertion, prometheus_vm_memory_collector, {151, 36, "8f0088"}, assert_type, "non_neg_integer()", proplist}.
%% memory_other/1: get_value(Key, Data) on what erlang:memory/0 gives, as in metrics/0: five sizes
{assertion, prometheus_vm_memory_collector, {167, 3, "f9cb84"}, assert_type, "non_neg_integer()", proplist}.
{assertion, prometheus_vm_memory_collector, {168, 7, "22cfc0"}, assert_type, "non_neg_integer()", proplist}.
{assertion, prometheus_vm_memory_collector, {169, 7, "3dda01"}, assert_type, "non_neg_integer()", proplist}.
{assertion, prometheus_vm_memory_collector, {170, 7, "f96ce6"}, assert_type, "non_neg_integer()", proplist}.
{assertion, prometheus_vm_memory_collector, {171, 7, "6e1ab1"}, assert_type, "non_neg_integer()", proplist}.
%% enabled_metrics/0: application:get_env(prometheus, vm_memory_collector_metrics, all), the names of the enabled
%% metrics or all. Type checked without it as long as the result of application:get_env/3 fitted every type
{assertion, prometheus_vm_memory_collector, {174, 3, "f328fd"}, assert_type, "all | [atom()]", app_env}.
%% metric_enabled/2: Metrics =:= all orelse lists:member(Name, Metrics): on the right of orelse Metrics is not all, so
%% it is the list
{assertion, prometheus_vm_memory_collector, {177, 45, "ca81d3"}, assert_type, "[atom()]", narrowing}.

{module, prometheus_vm_msacc_collector, #{file => "prometheus/src/collectors/vm/prometheus_vm_msacc_collector.erl",
                                          overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"},
                                                       {library, "overlay_prometheus_lib.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.
%% metrics/0: Data = erlang:statistics(microstate_accounting), which is undefined if the accounting is not available;
%% else a list with a map for each thread, the type that metric/3 takes
{assertion, prometheus_vm_msacc_collector, {206, 10, "e45f87"}, assert_type, "[#{type := atom(), id := non_neg_integer(), counters := #{atom() => non_neg_integer()}}]", unchecked_result}.
%% metrics/0: SecondAsPerfCounter = erlang:convert_time_unit(1, second, perf_counter), an integer() by its spec; metric/3
%% divides by it
{assertion, prometheus_vm_msacc_collector, {207, 25, "dbb893"}, assert_type, "pos_integer()", number_range}.
%% the spec has a map type with three mandatory associations, a thread of erlang:statistics(microstate_accounting)
{exception, prometheus_vm_msacc_collector, metric, 3, [ignore], map_types}.
%% enabled_metrics/0: application:get_env(prometheus, vm_msacc_collector_metrics, all), the names of the enabled metrics
%% or all. Type checked without it as long as the result of application:get_env/3 fitted every type
{assertion, prometheus_vm_msacc_collector, {273, 3, "4d91ec"}, assert_type, "all | [atom()]", app_env}.
%% metric_enabled/2: Metrics =:= all orelse lists:member(Name, Metrics): on the right of orelse Metrics is not all, so
%% it is the list
{assertion, prometheus_vm_msacc_collector, {276, 45, "ca81d3"}, assert_type, "[atom()]", narrowing}.

{module, prometheus_vm_statistics_collector, #{file => "prometheus/src/collectors/vm/prometheus_vm_statistics_collector.erl",
                                               overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"},
                                                            {library, "overlay_prometheus_lib.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.
%% metrics/0: [DirtyCPURunQueueLength, DirtyIORunQueueLength] = dirty_stat(), which gives a list of two
{assertion, prometheus_vm_statistics_collector, {160, 53, "4e2a61"}, assert_type, "etylizer:cons(non_neg_integer() | undefined, etylizer:cons(non_neg_integer() | undefined, []))", list_shape}.
%% enabled_metrics/0: application:get_env(prometheus, vm_statistics_collector_metrics, all), the names of the enabled
%% metrics or all. Type checked without it as long as the result of application:get_env/3 fitted every type
{assertion, prometheus_vm_statistics_collector, {227, 3, "84989e"}, assert_type, "all | [atom()]", app_env}.
%% metric_enabled/2: Metrics =:= all orelse lists:member(Name, Metrics): on the right of orelse Metrics is not all, so
%% it is the list
{assertion, prometheus_vm_statistics_collector, {230, 45, "ca81d3"}, assert_type, "[atom()]", narrowing}.

{module, prometheus_vm_system_info_collector, #{file => "prometheus/src/collectors/vm/prometheus_vm_system_info_collector.erl",
                                                overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"},
                                                             {library, "overlay_prometheus_lib.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.
%% collect_metrics/1: erlang:system_info(Name) for the name of a metric of metrics/0, an atom(): the 19 names that the
%% first two clauses leave, each of them an item of erlang:system_info/1 (for an item that an older release does not
%% know the call fails, which the function catches)
{assertion, prometheus_vm_system_info_collector, {299, 29, "d10743"}, assert_type, "dirty_cpu_schedulers | dirty_cpu_schedulers_online | dirty_io_schedulers | ets_limit | logical_processors | logical_processors_available | logical_processors_online | port_count | port_limit | process_count | process_limit | schedulers | schedulers_online | smp_support | threads | thread_pool_size | time_correction | atom_count | atom_limit", info_arg}.
%% enabled_metrics/0: application:get_env(prometheus, vm_system_info_collector_metrics, all), the names of the enabled
%% metrics or all. Type checked without it as long as the result of application:get_env/3 fitted every type
{assertion, prometheus_vm_system_info_collector, {308, 3, "fefb00"}, assert_type, "all | [atom()]", app_env}.
%% metric_enabled/2: Metrics =:= all orelse lists:member(Name, Metrics): on the right of orelse Metrics is not all, so
%% it is the list
{assertion, prometheus_vm_system_info_collector, {311, 45, "ca81d3"}, assert_type, "[atom()]", narrowing}.
%% collect_allocator_metrics/0: {Kind, KindInfo} <- Info for the kinds mbcs, mbcs_pool and sbcs of an allocator
%% instance: the information of a kind of carriers is a list of tuples, {blocks, ..}, {carriers, ..} and so on
{assertion, prometheus_vm_system_info_collector, {317, 62, "daa9df"}, assert_type, "[tuple()]", alloc_info}.
{assertion, prometheus_vm_system_info_collector, {320, 69, "daa9df"}, assert_type, "[tuple()]", alloc_info}.
%% allocator_metric/5: element(2, lists:keyfind(Key, 1, Values)), the current value of {carriers, Current,
%% MaxSinceLastCall, MaxEver} or of carriers_size in the information of one kind of carriers
{assertion, prometheus_vm_system_info_collector, {329, 9, "6428a9"}, assert_type, "non_neg_integer()", alloc_info}.
%% allocator_metric/5: lists:keyfind(Key, 1, Values) for the keys carriers and carriers_size, which the information of a
%% kind of carriers has
{assertion, prometheus_vm_system_info_collector, {329, 20, "c6617f"}, assert_type, "tuple()", unchecked_result}.
%% allocators/0: {_, N, Props} <- Allocs behind the filter Allocs =/= false: what erlang:system_info({allocator, A})
%% gives for an allocator that is enabled, {instance, N, Info} for each of its instances
{assertion, prometheus_vm_system_info_collector, {340, 26, "d5abde"}, assert_type, "[{instance, non_neg_integer(), [{atom(), term()}]}]", alloc_info}.
%% allocator_blocks_metric/5: lists:keyfind(blocks, 1, KindInfo): the information of a kind of carriers has the key
%% blocks, as {blocks, [{AllocatorType, [{count, N}, {size, N}]}]} or, in older releases, as {blocks, Current,
%% MaxSinceLastCall, MaxEver}
{assertion, prometheus_vm_system_info_collector, {343, 16, "801c31"}, assert_type, "tuple()", unchecked_result}.
%% allocator_blocks_metric/5: sum_alloc_block_list(count, L, 0) behind the guard is_list(L), which holds for an improper
%% list too
{assertion, prometheus_vm_system_info_collector, {345, 43, "22443f"}, assert_type, "[term()]", improper_list}.
%% allocator_blocks_metric/5: element(2, Tuple), the current number of blocks in the older form
{assertion, prometheus_vm_system_info_collector, {347, 15, "c12e29"}, assert_type, "non_neg_integer()", alloc_info}.
%% allocator_blocks_metric/5: element(2, lists:keyfind(blocks, 1, KindInfo)) where there is no key blocks_size: the list
%% of the newer form
{assertion, prometheus_vm_system_info_collector, {353, 47, "903cff"}, assert_type, "[term()]", alloc_info}.
%% allocator_blocks_metric/5: lists:keyfind(blocks, 1, KindInfo), as in the first clause
{assertion, prometheus_vm_system_info_collector, {353, 58, "801c31"}, assert_type, "tuple()", unchecked_result}.
%% allocator_blocks_metric/5: element(2, Tuple), the current size of {blocks_size, Current, MaxSinceLastCall, MaxEver}
{assertion, prometheus_vm_system_info_collector, {355, 20, "c12e29"}, assert_type, "non_neg_integer()", alloc_info}.
%% sum_alloc_block_list/3: an element {AllocatorType, L} of the list of blocks: L is its property list, [{count, N},
%% {size, N}]
{assertion, prometheus_vm_system_info_collector, {360, 41, "22443f"}, assert_type, "[tuple()]", alloc_info}.
%% sum_alloc_block_list/3: element(2, Tuple) for the {count, N} or {size, N} of an allocator type
{assertion, prometheus_vm_system_info_collector, {362, 24, "c12e29"}, assert_type, "non_neg_integer()", alloc_info}.

{module, prometheus_http, #{file => "prometheus/src/contrib/prometheus_http.erl",
                            overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.
%% the last clause, for what is not a positive integer: status_code() is pos_integer()
{exception, prometheus_http, status_class, 1, [no_redundancy], defensive}.

{module, prometheus_mnesia, #{file => "prometheus/src/contrib/prometheus_mnesia.erl",
                              overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"},
                                           {library, "overlay_prometheus_lib.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.
%% table_disk_size/1: mnesia:system_info(directory), the name of the directory of the database
{assertion, prometheus_mnesia, {25, 19, "1e76be"}, assert_type, "string()", info_item}.
{exception, prometheus_mnesia, tm_info, 0, [ignore], otp_no_spec}. % mnesia_tm:get_info/1

{module, prometheus_test_instrumenter, #{file => "prometheus/src/contrib/prometheus_test_instrumenter.erl",
                                         overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.

{module, prometheus_protobuf_format, #{file => "prometheus/src/formats/prometheus_protobuf_format.erl",
                                       overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.
{exception, prometheus_protobuf_format, format, 1, [ignore], otp_no_spec}. % ram_file:open/2, ram_file:get_size/1

{module, prometheus_text_format, #{file => "prometheus/src/formats/prometheus_text_format.erl",
                                   overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"},
                                                {library, "overlay_prometheus_lib.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.
{exception, prometheus_text_format, format, 1, [ignore], otp_no_spec}. % ram_file:open/2, ram_file:get_size/1
%% emit_mf_prologue/2: the fields name, type and help of a #'MetricFamily'{}, as prometheus_model_helpers:create_mf/4
%% writes them: the name and the help are text, the type one of the five atoms; the generated record also allows
%% undefined, and an integer() for the type
{assertion, prometheus_text_format, {91, 23, "d10743"}, assert_type, "iodata()", model_field}.
%% emit_mf_prologue/2: string_type(Type), "counter" and the like, a string() by its spec, in the iodata() for
%% file:write/2
{assertion, prometheus_text_format, {91, 34, "23cc12"}, assert_type, "[byte()]", text_bytes}.
{assertion, prometheus_text_format, {91, 46, "57a03f"}, assert_type, "prometheus_model:'MetricType'()", model_field}.
{assertion, prometheus_text_format, {92, 12, "d10743"}, assert_type, "iodata()", model_field}.
{assertion, prometheus_text_format, {92, 42, "aba8b9"}, assert_type, "iodata()", model_field}.
%% emit_mf_metrics/2: the fields name and metric of a #'MetricFamily'{}, the name and the list of the metrics; the
%% generated record also allows undefined
{assertion, prometheus_text_format, {97, 20, "d10743"}, assert_type, "iodata()", model_field}.
{assertion, prometheus_text_format, {97, 47, "ca81d3"}, assert_type, "[prometheus_model:'Metric'()]", model_field}.
%% no clause for a #'Metric'{} whose fields counter, gauge, untyped, summary and histogram are all undefined
{exception, prometheus_text_format, emit_metric, 3, [no_exhaustiveness], partial}.
%% emit_metric/3: the field label of a #'Metric'{}, the list of its labels, in each of the five clauses; the generated
%% record also allows undefined
{assertion, prometheus_text_format, {101, 56, "57316c"}, assert_type, "[prometheus_model:'LabelPair'()]", model_field}.
{assertion, prometheus_text_format, {104, 56, "57316c"}, assert_type, "[prometheus_model:'LabelPair'()]", model_field}.
{assertion, prometheus_text_format, {107, 56, "57316c"}, assert_type, "[prometheus_model:'LabelPair'()]", model_field}.
{assertion, prometheus_text_format, {112, 35, "57316c"}, assert_type, "[prometheus_model:'LabelPair'()]", model_field}.
%% emit_metric/3: io_lib:format("~p", [QN]), a quantile as text, for the field value of a #'LabelPair'{}, an iodata()
{assertion, prometheus_text_format, {120, 77, "16c2c2"}, assert_type, "iolist()", text_bytes}.
%% emit_metric/3: the field quantile of a #'Summary'{}, the list of its quantiles; the generated record also allows
%% undefined
{assertion, prometheus_text_format, {122, 50, "3553e9"}, assert_type, "[prometheus_model:'Quantile'()]", model_field}.
{assertion, prometheus_text_format, {128, 35, "57316c"}, assert_type, "[prometheus_model:'LabelPair'()]", model_field}.
%% emit_metric/3: the field bucket of a #'Histogram'{}, the list of its buckets; the generated record also allows
%% undefined
{assertion, prometheus_text_format, {130, 71, "fe3991"}, assert_type, "[prometheus_model:'Bucket'()]", model_field}.
%% emit_histogram_bucket/4: bound_to_label_value(BBound), the bound as integer_to_list/1 or float_to_list/1 print it, or
%% "+Inf": a string() by its spec, for the field value of a #'LabelPair'{}, an iodata()
{assertion, prometheus_text_format, {136, 13, "a2de26"}, assert_type, "[byte()]", text_bytes}.
%% emit_histogram_bucket/4: the field upper_bound of a #'Bucket'{}, a prometheus_buckets:bucket_bound() as
%% prometheus_model_helpers:histogram_metric/4 writes it; the generated record also allows '-infinity', nan and
%% undefined
{assertion, prometheus_text_format, {136, 34, "40e311"}, assert_type, "number() | infinity", model_field}.
%% [Name, "=\"", escape_label_value(Value), "\""] in the fun as iolist(): the field name of a #'LabelPair'{} is iodata()
%% | undefined, and text as prometheus_model_helpers:label_pair/1 writes it (model_field). A cast of the whole fun does
%% not help: its clause, which has the record as pattern, then counts as dead (seen in a scratch copy; here the hash
%% 06dca5 of the fun crashes the engine as well), and so it does with a cast of the variable Fun where it is used
{exception, prometheus_text_format, labels_stringify, 1, [ignore], in_fun}.
%% emit_series/4: io_lib:format("~p", [Value]), a float as text, in the iodata() for file:write/2
{assertion, prometheus_text_format, {167, 39, "f23566"}, assert_type, "iolist()", text_bytes}.
%% escape_string/2: Fun(X) for <<X:8>> <= Str: the fun takes a byte(), the segment of 8 bits is an integer()
{assertion, prometheus_text_format, {207, 13, "ed0a1f"}, assert_type, "byte()", bit_segment}.

{module, prometheus_boolean, #{file => "prometheus/src/metrics/prometheus_boolean.erl",
                               overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.
%% value/3: case ets:lookup(?TABLE, {Registry, Name, LabelValues}) of [{_Key, 0}] -> ..; [{_Key, 1}] -> ..; [{_Key,
%% undefined}] -> ..; [] -> .. end. The table is a set: no row, or the one of the series, {Key, 0 | 1 | undefined}
{assertion, prometheus_boolean, {249, 8, "657040"}, assert_type, "[] | etylizer:cons({{overlay_prometheus:registry(), overlay_prometheus:name(), overlay_prometheus:label_values()}, 0 | 1 | undefined}, [])", ets_value}.
%% values/2: [LabelValues, Value] <- load_all_values(Registry, Name), ets:match/2 on the rows {{Registry, Name,
%% LabelValues}, Value}. The call cannot carry the assertion (its hash 050cd9 crashes the engine), the variable can
{assertion, prometheus_boolean, {266, 27, "e2fb6b"}, assert_type, "overlay_prometheus:label_values()", ets_value}.
%% collect_mf/2: [Name, {Labels, Help}, CLabels, _, _] <- prometheus_metric:metrics(?TABLE, Registry). ets:match/2 gives
%% the bindings of a row as a list; the row of a metric family is the one that prometheus_metric:insert_mf/3 writes
{assertion, prometheus_boolean, {283, 46, "77c471"}, assert_type, "[etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:name(), etylizer:cons({[overlay_prometheus:label_name()], overlay_prometheus:help()}, etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:labels(), etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:duration_unit() | undefined, etylizer:cons(term(), [])))))]", ets_value}.
%% collect_metrics/2: [LabelValues, Value] <- load_all_values(Registry, Name), as in values/2: the label values and the
%% value of a row
{assertion, prometheus_boolean, {290, 35, "e2fb6b"}, assert_type, "overlay_prometheus:label_values()", ets_value}.
{assertion, prometheus_boolean, {290, 49, "2caa2e"}, assert_type, "0 | 1 | undefined", ets_value}.
%% insert_metric(Registry, Name, LabelValues, 0, fun toggle/3): insert_metric/5 calls the fun with four arguments if
%% another process has inserted the series meanwhile, toggle/3 takes three. In front of it: case ets:lookup(?TABLE, ..)
%% of [{_Key, undefined}] -> ..; [] -> .. end, which an assertion (ets_value) gets through
{exception, prometheus_boolean, save_toggle, 3, [ignore], source_bug}.

{module, prometheus_counter, #{file => "prometheus/src/metrics/prometheus_counter.erl",
                               overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"},
                                            {library, "overlay_prometheus_lib.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.
%% inc/4: case ets:select_replace(?TABLE, ..) of 0 -> ..; 1 -> ok end. The match specification names the key, the table
%% is a set: no row replaced, or one
{assertion, prometheus_counter, {194, 8, "873e6c"}, assert_type, "0 | 1", ets_value}.
%% value/3: ets:select/2 of '$1' + '$2' for the rows of the series, the sums of the two counters of a row
{assertion, prometheus_counter, {278, 8, "57773a"}, assert_type, "[number()]", ets_value}.
%% collect_mf/2: [Name, {Labels, Help}, CLabels, _, _] <- prometheus_metric:metrics(?TABLE, Registry). ets:match/2 gives
%% the bindings of a row as a list; the row of a metric family is the one that prometheus_metric:insert_mf/3 writes
{assertion, prometheus_counter, {309, 46, "43275b"}, assert_type, "[etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:name(), etylizer:cons({[overlay_prometheus:label_name()], overlay_prometheus:help()}, etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:labels(), etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:duration_unit() | undefined, etylizer:cons(term(), [])))))]", ets_value}.
%% reduce_label_values/1: MFValues is what load_all_values/2 gives, ets:match/2 on the rows {Key, ISum, FSum} of the
%% series: [LabelValues, ISum, FSum], the pattern of the fun for lists:foldl/3
{assertion, prometheus_counter, {356, 15, "a70f6a"}, assert_type, "[etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:label_values(), etylizer:cons(integer(), etylizer:cons(number(), [])))]", ets_value}.

{module, prometheus_gauge, #{file => "prometheus/src/metrics/prometheus_gauge.erl",
                             overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.
%% set/4: case Value of _ when is_number(Value) -> ..; undefined -> ..; _ -> erlang:error(..) end. The last branch is dead
%% for number() | undefined; with the subject annotated as a term(), which is checked, the checker takes it as reachable
{assertion, prometheus_gauge, {182, 10, "2caa2e"}, annotate_type, "term()", defensive}.
%% insert_metric(Registry, Name, LabelValues, Value, fun inc/4), as in maybe_insert_metric_for_inc/4. In front of it:
%% case ets:select_replace(?TABLE, ..) of 0 -> ..; 1 -> ok end, which an assertion 0 | 1 (ets_value) gets through.
%% Behind it: the last clause, dead for a number()
{exception, prometheus_gauge, inc, 4, [ignore], bounded_tyvar}.
%% the last clause, for a value that is neither a list nor a number
{exception, prometheus_gauge, dec, 2, [no_redundancy], defensive}.
{exception, prometheus_gauge, dec, 3, [no_redundancy], defensive}. % the last clause, for a value that is not a number
{exception, prometheus_gauge, dec, 4, [no_redundancy], defensive}. % the last clause, for a value that is not a number
{exception, prometheus_gauge, track_inprogress, 4, [no_redundancy], defensive}. % the last clause, for what is not a fun
{exception, prometheus_gauge, set_duration, 4, [no_redundancy], defensive}. % the last clause, for what is not a fun
%% sum(IValue, FValue) for [{_Key, IValue, FValue}] = ets:lookup(?TABLE, ..). A row is {Key, integer(), number()}, or
%% {Key, integer() | undefined, undefined} after set/4 with undefined. With the lookup asserted to be [] or one such row
%% (ets_value) the two variables are integer() | undefined and number() | undefined, and sum/2 has no clause for
%% undefined and a number
{exception, prometheus_gauge, value, 3, [ignore], union_elimination}.
%% sum(IValue, FValue) for [LabelValues, IValue, FValue] <- load_all_values(Registry, Name), as in value/3. Also: the
%% call load_all_values(Registry, Name) cannot carry an assertion, its hash 050cd9 crashes the engine
{exception, prometheus_gauge, values, 2, [ignore], union_elimination}.
%% collect_mf/2: [Name, {Labels, Help}, CLabels, DU, _] <- prometheus_metric:metrics(?TABLE, Registry). ets:match/2
%% gives the bindings of a row as a list; the row of a metric family is the one that prometheus_metric:insert_mf/3
%% writes
{assertion, prometheus_gauge, {445, 47, "642edc"}, assert_type, "[etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:name(), etylizer:cons({[overlay_prometheus:label_name()], overlay_prometheus:help()}, etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:labels(), etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:duration_unit() | undefined, etylizer:cons(term(), [])))))]", ets_value}.
%% sum(IValue, FValue) for [LabelValues, IValue, FValue] <- load_all_values(Registry, Name), as in value/3 and values/2
{exception, prometheus_gauge, collect_metrics, 2, [ignore], union_elimination}.
%% insert_metric(Registry, Name, LabelValues, Value, fun inc/4): the spec of insert_metric/5 has Value :: number() |
%% undefined for the value and for the argument of the fun, inc/4 takes a number()
{exception, prometheus_gauge, maybe_insert_metric_for_inc, 4, [ignore], bounded_tyvar}.

{module, prometheus_histogram, #{file => "prometheus/src/metrics/prometheus_histogram.erl",
                                 overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"},
                                              {library, "overlay_prometheus_lib.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.
%% deregister/2: Buckets = prometheus_metric:mf_data(MF). The data of a histogram are its buckets, which
%% validate_histogram_spec/1 has put under the key data of the spec
{assertion, prometheus_histogram, {164, 15, "65dcbe"}, assert_type, "prometheus_buckets:buckets()", mf_data}.
%% deregister/2: MF = prometheus_metric:check_mf_exists(?TABLE, Registry, Name), which is false for an unknown metric:
%% mf_data/1 fails for it and the try around makes {false, false} of that
{assertion, prometheus_histogram, {164, 41, "5df1ff"}, assert_type, "overlay_prometheus:mf()", unchecked_result}.
%% for a float and a series that exists the result is the one of fobserve_impl/3, the 0 or 1 of ets:select_replace/2,
%% and not ok as in the other clauses. In front of it: case ets:lookup(?TABLE, Key) of [Metric] -> ..; [] -> .. end,
%% twice, which an assertion (ets_value) gets through
{exception, prometheus_histogram, observe, 4, [ignore], source_bug}.
%% for a float and a series that is new the result is the one of the fun given to insert_metric/5, fobserve_impl/4 with
%% the 0 or 1 of ets:select_replace/2, and not ok. In front of it: case fobserve_impl(Key, Buckets, BucketPos, Value) of
%% 0 -> ..; 1 -> ok end, which wants an assertion 0 | 1 (ets_value) on the call, whose hash 028dfe crashes the engine
%% (seen with the clause 1 changed to _ in a scratch copy)
{exception, prometheus_histogram, pobserve, 6, [ignore], source_bug}.
%% the last clause, for what is not a fun
{exception, prometheus_histogram, observe_duration, 4, [no_redundancy], defensive}.
%% reset/3: Buckets = prometheus_metric:mf_data(MF), the buckets of the histogram
{assertion, prometheus_histogram, {320, 13, "65dcbe"}, assert_type, "prometheus_buckets:buckets()", mf_data}.
%% value/3: the counters of the buckets, one for each bound of the histogram, and a histogram has the bound infinity at
%% least
{assertion, prometheus_histogram, {359, 16, "2a146c"}, assert_type, "[number(), ...]", nonempty_list}.
%% buckets/3: prometheus_metric:mf_data(MF), the buckets of the histogram
{assertion, prometheus_histogram, {381, 3, "65dcbe"}, assert_type, "prometheus_buckets:buckets()", mf_data}.
%% deregister_cleanup/1: [_, _, _, _, Buckets] <- prometheus_metric:metrics(?TABLE, Registry). ets:match/2 gives the
%% bindings of a row as a list; the row of a metric family is the one that prometheus_metric:insert_mf/3 writes, its
%% data the buckets of the histogram
{assertion, prometheus_histogram, {390, 32, "83a7c7"}, assert_type, "[etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:name(), etylizer:cons({[overlay_prometheus:label_name()], overlay_prometheus:help()}, etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:labels(), etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:duration_unit() | undefined, etylizer:cons(prometheus_buckets:buckets(), [])))))]", ets_value}.
%% collect_mf/2: [Name, {Labels, Help}, CLabels, DU, Buckets] <- prometheus_metric:metrics(?TABLE, Registry), as in
%% deregister_cleanup/1
{assertion, prometheus_histogram, {398, 10, "83a7c7"}, assert_type, "[etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:name(), etylizer:cons({[overlay_prometheus:label_name()], overlay_prometheus:help()}, etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:labels(), etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:duration_unit() | undefined, etylizer:cons(prometheus_buckets:buckets(), [])))))]", ets_value}.
%% validate_histogram_spec/1: RBuckets = prometheus_metric_spec:get_value(buckets, Spec, default), what the key buckets
%% of the spec can be; prometheus_buckets:new/1 raises an error for other values
{assertion, prometheus_histogram, {418, 36, "55092f"}, assert_type, "overlay_prometheus:buckets_spec()", proplist}.
%% insert_placeholders/3: MFBuckets = prometheus_metric:mf_data(MF), the buckets of the histogram
{assertion, prometheus_histogram, {444, 15, "65dcbe"}, assert_type, "prometheus_buckets:buckets()", mf_data}.
%% generate_select_replace/4: ?BUCKETS_START + BucketPos, 5 + non_neg_integer(), as the pos_integer() that
%% gen_query_placeholder/1 takes
{assertion, prometheus_histogram, {463, 52, "a3592c"}, assert_type, "pos_integer()", arith_range}.
%% metric_buckets/1: element(?BOUNDS_POS, Metric). The row of a series is {Key, Bounds, ISum, FSum, Counter1, ..}, as
%% insert_placeholders/3 writes it: the bounds of the buckets in native units, the two sums and a counter for each
%% bucket
{assertion, prometheus_histogram, {491, 3, "46cd45"}, assert_type, "prometheus_buckets:buckets()", ets_value}.
%% reduce_buckets_counters/1: ?BUCKETS_START + length(..), 5 + non_neg_integer(), as the pos_integer() that
%% sub_tuple_to_list/3 takes
{assertion, prometheus_histogram, {496, 39, "e7a755"}, assert_type, "pos_integer()", arith_range}.
%% reduce_buckets_counters/1: for each row the elements from ?BUCKETS_START on, the counters of its buckets;
%% sub_tuple_to_list/3 gives the elements of a tuple as terms
{assertion, prometheus_histogram, {498, 45, "acf905"}, assert_type, "[[non_neg_integer()]]", ets_value}.
{exception, prometheus_histogram, transpose, 1, [ignore], bif_fun}. % lists:map(fun hd/1, M), lists:map(fun tl/1, M)
%% reduce_sum/1: element(?ISUM_POS, Metric) + element(?FSUM_POS, Metric), the two sums of a row: the sum of the integers
%% observed and the sum of the floats
{assertion, prometheus_histogram, {505, 14, "f79149"}, assert_type, "integer()", ets_value}.
{assertion, prometheus_histogram, {505, 43, "6d2538"}, assert_type, "number()", ets_value}.
%% the last argument is [ISum, FSum | Buckets]: no clause for a list of less than two
{exception, prometheus_histogram, create_histogram_metric, 6, [no_exhaustiveness], list_shape}.
%% create_histogram_metric/6: the list is [ISum, FSum | Buckets], two sums, which are numbers, and the counters of the
%% buckets, which are not negative integers; so are the cumulative counters that augment_counters/1 makes of them,
%% [number(), ...] by its spec
{assertion, prometheus_histogram, {513, 15, "e889f1"}, assert_type, "[non_neg_integer(), ...]", list_shape}.
%% create_histogram_metric/6: Buckets, one counter for each bound of the histogram, and a histogram has the bound
%% infinity at least
{assertion, prometheus_histogram, {513, 32, "fe3991"}, assert_type, "[number(), ...]", nonempty_list}.
%% sub_tuple_to_list/3: Pos + 1, pos_integer() + 1, as the pos_integer() of the function itself
{assertion, prometheus_histogram, {542, 55, "86fcca"}, assert_type, "pos_integer()", arith_range}.
%% reduce_label_values/1: MFValues is what load_all_values/3 gives, ets:match/2 on the rows of the series: [LabelValues,
%% ISum, FSum, Counter1, ..], the pattern [Labels | V] of the fun for lists:foldl/3
{assertion, prometheus_histogram, {560, 15, "a70f6a"}, assert_type, "[etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:label_values(), [number()])]", ets_value}.
%% mf_values/3: Bounds = prometheus_metric:mf_data(MF), the buckets of the histogram
{assertion, prometheus_histogram, {565, 12, "65dcbe"}, assert_type, "prometheus_buckets:buckets()", mf_data}.
%% mf_values/3: the values of the map of reduce_label_values/1 are [ISum, FSum | BCounters], the pattern of the fun for
%% maps:fold/3: a list that starts with the two sums
{assertion, prometheus_histogram, {577, 14, "96b51c"}, assert_type, "#{overlay_prometheus:label_values() => etylizer:cons(number(), etylizer:cons(number(), [number()]))}", ets_value}.

{module, prometheus_quantile_summary, #{file => "prometheus/src/metrics/prometheus_quantile_summary.erl",
                                        overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"},
                                                     {library, "overlay_prometheus_lib.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.
%% set_default/2: #{compress_limit := CompressLimit} = Configuration, a qs_config(), which has the key
{assertion, prometheus_quantile_summary, {152, 3, "474f7c"}, assert_pattern, "#{compress_limit := _}", map_types}.
%% case ets:lookup(?TABLE, Key) of [] -> ..; [{Key, Count, S, Q, CompressLimit}] -> .. end with Key bound: also with the
%% lookup asserted to be [] or one row {Key, Count, Sum, Estimator, CompressLimit} (ets_value) the case counts as not
%% exhaustive
{exception, prometheus_quantile_summary, observe, 4, [ignore], bound_pattern}.
%% the last clause, for what is not a fun
{exception, prometheus_quantile_summary, observe_duration, 4, [no_redundancy], defensive}.
%% reset/3: Configuration = prometheus_metric:mf_data(MF). The data of a quantile summary is its configuration, the map
%% that validate_summary_spec/1 has put under the key data of the spec
{assertion, prometheus_quantile_summary, {258, 19, "65dcbe"}, assert_type, "overlay_prometheus:qs_config()", mf_data}.
%% value/3: #{quantiles := QNs} = prometheus_metric:mf_data(MF): the pattern on the configuration, a qs_config(), which
%% has the key
{assertion, prometheus_quantile_summary, {291, 3, "8a9811"}, assert_pattern, "#{quantiles := _}", map_types}.
%% value/3: prometheus_metric:mf_data(MF), the configuration of the quantile summary
{assertion, prometheus_quantile_summary, {291, 25, "65dcbe"}, assert_type, "overlay_prometheus:qs_config()", mf_data}.
%% value/3: ets:select/2 of '$$' for the rows {Key, Count, Sum, Estimator, CompressLimit} of the series: [Count, Sum,
%% Estimator] for each
{assertion, prometheus_quantile_summary, {293, 8, "5888d9"}, assert_type, "[etylizer:cons(non_neg_integer(), etylizer:cons(number(), etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:estimator(), [])))]", ets_value}.
%% values/2: #{quantiles := QNs} = Configuration = prometheus_metric:mf_data(MF): the pattern on the configuration, a
%% qs_config(), which has the key
{assertion, prometheus_quantile_summary, {307, 7, "4a75f5"}, assert_pattern, "#{quantiles := _}", map_types}.
%% values/2: prometheus_metric:mf_data(MF), the configuration of the quantile summary
{assertion, prometheus_quantile_summary, {307, 45, "65dcbe"}, assert_type, "overlay_prometheus:qs_config()", mf_data}.
%% values/2: MFValues = load_all_values(Registry, Name), ets:match/2 on the rows {Key, Count, Sum, Estimator,
%% CompressLimit} of the series: [LabelValues, Count, Sum, Estimator], the pattern of the fun for lists:foldl/3. The
%% call cannot carry the assertion (its hash 050cd9 crashes the engine), the variable can
{assertion, prometheus_quantile_summary, {316, 7, "a70f6a"}, assert_type, "[etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:label_values(), etylizer:cons(non_neg_integer(), etylizer:cons(number(), etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:estimator(), []))))]", ets_value}.
%% collect_mf/2: [Name, {Labels, Help}, CLabels, DU, Data] <- prometheus_metric:metrics(?TABLE, Registry). ets:match/2
%% gives the bindings of a row as a list; the row of a metric family is the one that prometheus_metric:insert_mf/3
%% writes, its data the configuration of the quantile summary
{assertion, prometheus_quantile_summary, {341, 50, "9b8b2d"}, assert_type, "[etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:name(), etylizer:cons({[overlay_prometheus:label_name()], overlay_prometheus:help()}, etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:labels(), etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:duration_unit() | undefined, etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:qs_config(), [])))))]", ets_value}.
%% collect_metrics/2: #{quantiles := QNs} = Configuration, a qs_config(), which has the key
{assertion, prometheus_quantile_summary, {347, 3, "36cffd"}, assert_pattern, "#{quantiles := _}", map_types}.
%% collect_metrics/2: MFValues = load_all_values(Registry, Name), as in values/2
{assertion, prometheus_quantile_summary, {355, 7, "a70f6a"}, assert_type, "[etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:label_values(), etylizer:cons(non_neg_integer(), etylizer:cons(number(), etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:estimator(), []))))]", ets_value}.
%% insert_metric/5: Configuration = prometheus_metric:mf_data(MF), the configuration of the quantile summary
{assertion, prometheus_quantile_summary, {398, 19, "65dcbe"}, assert_type, "overlay_prometheus:qs_config()", mf_data}.
%% insert_metric/5: #{compress_limit := CompressLimit} = Configuration, a qs_config(), which has the key
{assertion, prometheus_quantile_summary, {399, 3, "474f7c"}, assert_pattern, "#{compress_limit := _}", map_types}.
%% get_configuration/2: prometheus_metric:mf_data(MF), the configuration of the quantile summary
{assertion, prometheus_quantile_summary, {414, 3, "65dcbe"}, assert_type, "overlay_prometheus:qs_config()", mf_data}.
%% get_configuration/2: MF = prometheus_metric:check_mf_exists(?TABLE, Registry, Name), which is false for an unknown
%% metric; set_default/2 asks for the configuration of the metric that prometheus_metric:insert_mf/3 has just inserted
{assertion, prometheus_quantile_summary, {414, 29, "5df1ff"}, assert_type, "overlay_prometheus:mf()", unchecked_result}.
%% reduce_values/1: Values are the rows of the schedulers for one series, each as [Count, Sum, Estimator]: a list of
%% elements of different types, [number() | estimator()] by the spec; the three comprehensions take a row apart
{assertion, prometheus_quantile_summary, {425, 33, "a7ed06"}, assert_type, "[etylizer:cons(non_neg_integer(), etylizer:cons(number(), etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:estimator(), [])))]", ets_value}.
{assertion, prometheus_quantile_summary, {426, 33, "a7ed06"}, assert_type, "[etylizer:cons(non_neg_integer(), etylizer:cons(number(), etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:estimator(), [])))]", ets_value}.
%% reduce_values/1: the estimators of the rows, for fold_quantiles/1, which takes a list that is not empty: value/3
%% calls reduce_values/1 only for rows that ets:select/2 has found
{assertion, prometheus_quantile_summary, {427, 19, "9f6866"}, assert_type, "[overlay_prometheus:estimator(), ...]", nonempty_list}.
%% quantile_estimator:f_targeted(Targets) takes a list that is not empty: the fun it gives fails for no targets
%% (lists:min([])). validate_targets/1 accepts [], so a summary with {targets, []} is declared and fails at an
%% observation. In front of it: lists:unzip(Targets) for the term() of the key targets, which validate_targets/1 has
%% checked to be pairs of floats (an assertion, validated, gets through)
{exception, prometheus_quantile_summary, invariant_and_quantiles_from_spec, 1, [ignore], source_bug}.
%% compress_limit_from_spec/1: the key compress_limit of the spec, the number of inserts after which the estimator is
%% compressed
{assertion, prometheus_quantile_summary, {442, 3, "dbe8ea"}, assert_type, "integer()", proplist}.
%% validate_targets/1: lists:foreach(.., Targets) behind the guard is_list(Targets)
{assertion, prometheus_quantile_summary, {456, 5, "5789a7"}, assert_type, "[term()]", improper_list}.
%% the clause quantile(#{invariant := Invariant}) for a qs_config(), which has the key
{exception, prometheus_quantile_summary, quantile, 1, [no_exhaustiveness], map_types}.
%% fold_quantiles/1: lists:foldl(fun (Q, init) -> Q; (Q1, Q2) -> quantile_merge(Q1, Q2) end, init, QList). The result is
%% init only for the empty list, and QList is not empty
{assertion, prometheus_quantile_summary, {483, 3, "7d0355"}, assert_type, "overlay_prometheus:estimator()", nonempty_list}.
%% #quantile_estimator{samples_count = .., data = .., invariant = ..}: data_count and inserts_since_compression are left
%% undefined, their types are number() and non_neg_integer(). The source has -dialyzer({nowarn_function,
%% quantile_merge/2}) for it
{exception, prometheus_quantile_summary, quantile_merge, 2, [ignore], missing_fields}.

{module, prometheus_summary, #{file => "prometheus/src/metrics/prometheus_summary.erl",
                               overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"},
                                            {library, "overlay_prometheus_lib.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.
%% the last clause, for a value that is not a number
{exception, prometheus_summary, observe, 4, [no_redundancy], defensive}.
%% observe/4: case ets:select_replace(?TABLE, ..) of 0 -> ..; 1 -> ok end. The match specification names the key, the
%% table is a set: no row replaced, or one
{assertion, prometheus_summary, {167, 5, "d29284"}, assert_type, "0 | 1", ets_value}.
%% the last clause, for what is not a fun
{exception, prometheus_summary, observe_duration, 4, [no_redundancy], defensive}.
%% value/3: ets:select/2 of '$$' for the rows {Key, Count, ISum, FSum} of the series: [Count, ISum, FSum] for each
{assertion, prometheus_summary, {282, 8, "9e2449"}, assert_type, "[etylizer:cons(non_neg_integer(), etylizer:cons(integer(), etylizer:cons(number(), [])))]", ets_value}.
%% values/2: MFValues = load_all_values(Registry, Name), ets:match/2 on the rows {Key, Count, ISum, FSum} of the series:
%% [LabelValues, Count, ISum, FSum], the pattern of the fun for lists:foldl/3. The call cannot carry the assertion (its
%% hash 050cd9 crashes the engine), the variable can
{assertion, prometheus_summary, {303, 7, "a70f6a"}, assert_type, "[etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:label_values(), etylizer:cons(non_neg_integer(), etylizer:cons(integer(), etylizer:cons(number(), []))))]", ets_value}.
%% collect_mf/2: [Name, {Labels, Help}, CLabels, DU, _] <- prometheus_metric:metrics(?TABLE, Registry). ets:match/2
%% gives the bindings of a row as a list; the row of a metric family is the one that prometheus_metric:insert_mf/3
%% writes
{assertion, prometheus_summary, {327, 47, "205ede"}, assert_type, "[etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:name(), etylizer:cons({[overlay_prometheus:label_name()], overlay_prometheus:help()}, etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:labels(), etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:duration_unit() | undefined, etylizer:cons(term(), [])))))]", ets_value}.
%% collect_metrics/2: MFValues = load_all_values(Registry, Name), as in values/2
{assertion, prometheus_summary, {340, 7, "a70f6a"}, assert_type, "[etylizer:cons(overlay_prometheus:label_values(), etylizer:cons(non_neg_integer(), etylizer:cons(integer(), etylizer:cons(number(), []))))]", ets_value}.

{module, prometheus_model_helpers, #{file => "prometheus/src/model/prometheus_model_helpers.erl",
                                     overlays => [{specs, "overlay_prometheus.erl"},
                                                  {library, "overlay_prometheus_lib.erl"}], timeout => 10000}}.
%% metric_name/1: case is_atom(P) of true -> atom_to_binary(P, utf8); _ -> P end for an element P of the name: P is an
%% atom in the first branch and none in the second
{assertion, prometheus_model_helpers, {91, 33, "790b52"}, assert_type, "atom()", narrowing}.
{assertion, prometheus_model_helpers, {92, 15, "790b52"}, assert_type, "byte() | iolist() | binary()", narrowing}.
%% metric_from_tuple/2: Metric behind the guard is_record(Metric, 'Metric'), which narrows it to tuple() only
{assertion, prometheus_model_helpers, {363, 3, "7965d7"}, assert_type, "prometheus_model:'Metric'()", record_guard}.
%% metric_from_tuple/2: the six clauses for a metric that is no record: Metric is a tmetric() of the kind that the first
%% argument names, the type of the metric family for which prometheus_model_helpers:create_mf/4 has been given it
{assertion, prometheus_model_helpers, {365, 16, "7965d7"}, assert_type, "gauge()", correlated}.
{assertion, prometheus_model_helpers, {367, 18, "7965d7"}, assert_type, "counter()", correlated}.
{assertion, prometheus_model_helpers, {369, 18, "7965d7"}, assert_type, "pbool()", correlated}.
{assertion, prometheus_model_helpers, {371, 18, "7965d7"}, assert_type, "summary()", correlated}.
{assertion, prometheus_model_helpers, {373, 20, "7965d7"}, assert_type, "histogram()", correlated}.
{assertion, prometheus_model_helpers, {375, 18, "7965d7"}, assert_type, "untyped()", correlated}.
%% ensure_list(Val) when is_list(Val) -> Val, as a [T]: a T that is itself a list comes back as it is. For create_mf/4 T
%% has such values: a pbool() can be a list (prometheus_boolean()), which is then taken for a list of metrics
{exception, prometheus_model_helpers, ensure_list, 1, [ignore], source_bug}.
%% the clause when is_list(Val) gives back any list as text (binary() | iolist()), the source says FIXME: validate utf8.
%% A label value or a help that is a list but no iodata() fails later, in iolist_to_binary/1 of the text format
{exception, prometheus_model_helpers, ensure_binary_or_string, 1, [ignore], source_bug}.
